A||||15||RiceCooker||A Timeline - How would you feel?.........||||13||
Z||000000||RiceCooker||05-03-2001||02:17 PM||||Here is my tale of woe. Just would like to see how many people here would remain patient after the follwing story, and how many people would be absolutly furious.<P>4/6/01: <BR>- Problem is discovered after clutch & slave cylinders are replaced - the clutch release lever was bent and is now broken. This and the slave were both faulty and the cause of my problems. Mechanic talks to GM and they do not carry this part anymore, it's off their books. Over the weekend i gather some info on this part so i know exactly what i'm looking for.<P>4/8/01 PM & 4/9/01 AM:<BR>- Sent out approx ten emails looking for my part. Here is the email:<P>""Hi,<P>My name's Todd and i'm in need of a clutch release lever for my 86se V6 4spd. I found out AFTER i had replaced both slave and master  cylinders that mine had bent and had been causing my clutch problems.<P> Just for specifics the part is: - chilton's pg. 7-57, fig. 70 #2<BR>- Haynes pg. 189, fig. 3.1 #2<P> My car is currently out of commission so if you have this part, please get back to me asap. I will need it UPS overnight service.<P>Thanks so much,<BR>Todd<P>aka RiceCooker""<P>Note how specific i was providing even the page #'s of the pictures of this part to avoid a possible confusion.<P>I received various emails that morning including one from *********. This was the only one that could actually send the parton that day and it was an actual fiero business so i figured i couldnt go wrong. ****** at ****** sent me his # so i called.<P>4/9/01 PM:<BR>- talked to ****** @ *******. They have the part and will send it for me overnight. I paid by visa for the part and was ecited to be near the end of my problems.<P>4/10/01:<BR>- No word<P>4/11/01:<BR>- No part, I phoned ***** and the part is still there. The UPS guy couldnt/wouldnt pick it up. It will go out today. Tracking # provided.<P>4/12/01 to 4/16/01:<BR>- Tracked Package on internet (Very cool by the way) until it arrived monday morning. Overnight service will not be overnight during Canadian holiday long weekend. That's ok, i'm still patient.<P>4/16/01:<BR>- Talked to my mechanic. I just got a shiny new clutch PEDAL.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Tough break, eh?<BR>I phone ****** that afternoon and no answer so i leave a message.<P>4/17/01:<BR>- Talked to *****. He apologized for the mistake, i was confused how i could get the wrong part even after i was very specific. I find out to my surprise that they dont have the Haynes or Chilton's manuals. We talk about the real part that i need. They have it and not sure on price. Probably $7*.** something but we'll call it an even 50 and charge my visa the diff. Sounds OK to me. I have not even gotten upset yet. I remain patient and understanding. I have worked in sales before and i hate a$$hole customers. The part will go out today or tommorrow.<P>4/24/01:<BR>- Clutch pedal sent back to *******. <P>4/25/01: <BR>- No word or no part as of yet. No answer at ***** so an email is sent requesting Tracking # (this email still has not been replyed to) <P>4/26/01: <BR>- phone *****. "Oh sh**. yeah i have it here" No apologies just excuses given. I'm confused as to why the part is right there and has not been sent, more than a week later. It will be sent out right away. I ask for an email for confirmation and tracking as soon as it goes out. I am upset, but i remain calm.<P>5/3/01:<BR>- Still no email, no word, no part from *******. I have paid for a months insurnace on my car while it has sat in the shop, waiting for a part that could have been here 3 weeks ago. And yes this is my daily driver and i do not have another vehicle.<P><BR>I understand that people have busy lives and circumstances arise. Life is even more difficult when you dont have your car to get around. I dont mind if things come up, but to be told again and again that this part will be "on it's way" and it's not, is just plain old being lied to.<P>We all have busy days. <BR>Excuses are like a$$holes<BR>-everybody has one<BR>-they all stink<P>How would you feel in this situation?<BR>I do beleive i NOW have the right to be angry after being patient for almost a month i am ready to explode.<P>I have not revealed the vendor or the person in this case. Depending on what happens in our phone conversation this afternoon, i may reveal it after i tear a strip off him on the phone. Perhaps he will be apopogetic and realize the mistake and i will get the part for free. I will now be looking for the part elsewhere and will never deal with ******** again regardless. I will keep you updated.<P>Sorry for the long post and thanks for listening<BR>Todd<P> <P>------------------<BR>This is my witty signature,<BR>It makes me cool<p>[This message has been edited by RiceCooker (edited 05-03-2001).]||||reg||13
